#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-interface.md:2
msgid "gpio interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-interface.md:4
msgid ""
"`gpio` allows access to a specific GPIO pin. The interface is restricted "
"because it provides privileged access to GPIO hardware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-interface.md:7
msgid ""
"Use  `snap interface gpio` to see which gpio devices are available on the "
"system:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-interface.md:9
msgid ""
"$ snap interface gpio\n"
"name:    gpio\n"
"summary: allows access to a specific GPIO pin\n"
"slots:\n"
"  - pi:bcm-gpio-0\n"
"  - pi:bcm-gpio-1\n"
"  - pi:bcm-gpio-10\n"
"[...]\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-interface.md:20
msgid "<h2 id='heading--example'>Example</h2>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-interface.md:22
msgid ""
"The [pi-fancontrol](https://snapcraft.io/pi-fancontrol) snap provides simple "
"fan control on a Raspberry Pi with a fan connected to GPIO 14 (pin 8). With "
"the snap installed, the following command will connect the interface to the "
"pin:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-interface.md:24
msgid "snap connect pi-fancontrol:gpio pi:bcm-gpio-14\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-interface.md:29
msgid "Developer details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-interface.md:31
msgid "**Auto-connect**: no</br> **Attributes**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-interface.md:31
msgid "</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-interface.md:33
msgid ""
"`number` (slot): GPIO pin number to export and expose to consuming snaps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-interface.md:35
msgid ""
"Hardware IO interfaces covers some general considerations common to these "
"kinds of devices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-interface.md:37
msgid ""
"To use a gpio device, the snap developer must add `plugs: [ gpio ]` to a "
"snap's [snapcraft.yaml](https://documentation.ubuntu.com/snapcraft/stable/"
"reference/project-file/anatomy-of-snapcraft-yaml/). The snap user can then "
"access a specific gpio device with an {ref}`interface connection "
"<explanation-interfaces-all-about-interfaces>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-interface.md:39
msgid ""
"Unless the snap is expected to actually use a set of gpio pins that is not "
"predefined,  it is recommended to define distinct plugs for each used gpio "
"pin, like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-interface.md:41
msgid ""
"plugs:\n"
"  activity-led:\n"
"    interface: gpio\n"
"  warning-led:\n"
"    interface: gpio\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-interface.md:49
msgid ""
"This has the advantage of being self-documenting and 1-1  connections like "
"these are easier to track and setup with {ref}`auto-connections <explanation-"
"interfaces-interface-auto-connection>`, if the latter is needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-interface.md:51
msgid ""
"When the interface is connected, `\"echo (pin number) > /sys/class/gpio/"
"export\"`  is run internally to enable access to the GPIO pin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-interface.md:53
msgid ""
"Once connected, the consuming snap can use the device via `/sys/class/gpio/"
"gpioN` where `N` is the pin number specified by the connected slot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-interface.md:55
msgid ""
"Finally, when the interface is disconnected,  `\"echo (pin number) > /sys/"
"class/gpio/unexport\"`  is run internally to disable access to the GPIO pin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-interface.md:57
msgid "Code examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-interface.md:59
msgid ""
"The hook and control scripts for _pi-fancontrol_ can be found in the "
"project's GitHub repository: [https://github.com/ogra1/pi-fancontrol-snap]"
"(https://github.com/ogra1/pi-fancontrol-snap)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/gpio-interface.md:61
msgid ""
"The source code for the GPIO interface is in the _snapd_ repository: "
"[https://github.com/canonical/snapd/blob/master/interfaces/builtin/gpio.go]"
"(https://github.com/canonical/snapd/blob/master/interfaces/builtin/gpio.go)."
msgstr ""
